    {
      "type": "intro",
      "heading": "Verbs run the sentence",
      "body": "In Punjabi the verb is the anchor — it always sits at the end of the sentence and carries a lot of information, including whether the subject is masculine or feminine.\n\nThis lesson gives you the ten most useful everyday verbs, the \"to do something\" infinitive form, and your first full present-tense sentence pattern: main X-da/X-di haan."
    },
